# Frontend build-time configuration (Vite inlines anything VITE_-prefixed).
#
# All three values are PUBLIC by design — they ship inside the JS bundle that
# every visitor downloads. They are addresses and identifiers, not credentials:
# the API URL says where to send requests, and the Cognito ids say which user
# pool to authenticate against. Neither grants anything on its own.
#
# Security comes from the Cognito signature check on every request and from
# Postgres Row-Level Security behind it — never from hiding these.
#
# NEVER put here: a Cognito app-client SECRET, a database password, or an AWS
# access key. The app client for this frontend must be created WITHOUT a client
# secret (a browser cannot keep one), and the CodeBuild step greps the built
# bundle for these patterns and fails the build.

VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:7869
VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=ap-south-1_XXXXXXXXX
VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=your_cognito_app_client_id
